{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter","id":388724,"title":"Dark Eras Neolithic Chapter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-01T12:26:20-08:00","id":388724,"title":"Dark Eras Neolithic Chapter","content":"Guys! Go vote for<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dark-eras-poll/\" target=\"_blank\"> Neolithic Mages.<br /> <br /> I</a>'m really curious to see how that turns out - so much of the setting culture would need to be dropped or adjusted. At the same time, &quot;Atlantis&quot; (Babel, Shamballah, Kumari Kandam, Atzlan - whatever) was a preexisting reality, so it's shadow in theory should still hold in this linear past.... strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:38:07-08:00","id":388758,"title":"","content":"Mage is typically one of my least-favorite gamelines, but these Dark Eras are knocking it out of the park, much moreso than for the games I actually like. Bravo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:47:21-08:00","id":388767,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue, helvetica, arial, lucida grande, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I love <b>Mage</b>, but <b>Werewolf</b> need it's love also. As mine modern <b>Wolfs</b> game is set on the North of Sweden, on the ruins of old werewolf-Vikings settlement, I feel a game need more mine vote. Especially, as original setting for <b>Werewolf</b>, 1970s New York, is a bit joke, in comparison with <b>Mage</b> one <i>To The Strongest</i>. So mine vote goes to Viking werewolves, but if it will lost, I win also with <b>Mage</b> one Era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2015, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T12:59:16-08:00","id":388784,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Scelesti will feature prominently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/