target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:24:23-08:00","id":388818,"title":"","content":"Within the context of the dark era there wasn't much done for them. The section on the idigam will probably be a sidebar in the proper book. Bowery Dogs was more about being a punk and fighting against oppression.<br /> <br /> And the Idigam are divided into two groups, the Eartbound and the Moon-Banished. The Earthbound have been here for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:16:26-08:00","id":388912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=388818#post388818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within the context of the dark era there wasn't much done for them. The section on the idigam will probably be a sidebar in the proper book. Bowery Dogs was more about being a punk and fighting against oppression.<br /> <br /> And the Idigam are divided into two groups, the Eartbound and the Moon-Banished. The Earthbound have been here for a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really get the that 1970s New York can reason with <b>Werewolf</b> game, really. But <b>To The Strongest</b> is game changing Era for <b>Mage</b>, where future Orders-to-be are making first exchanges. In context of <b>Werewolf</b>, I think Viking era of conquest and pagan worshiping wolf gods fighting with Christanity is much more important. I would not be surprised it was one of the turning points for Blood Talons history also, with all the Fenris guidance.<br /> <br /> It's like comparing 1700s Carbean <b>Mage</b> with <b>To The Strongest </b>- both are suitable Eras for game. But <b>To The Strongst</b> is so much more important for the gameline. I even think that Neolithic <b>Mage</b> could be next one, followed by Renaissance <b>Mage</b> one ( just after Ministry reforms). But <b>Mage</b> already have <b>To The Stongest</b> super chapter. And <b>Werewolf</b> have only black punk wolves in New York in Dark Eras. <br /> <br /> As a side note - my cWerewolf RPG club friends point that Dark Ages WtA were so great and Forsaken lacks this kind of history. Please, help me make them wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T14:52:08-08:00","id":388968,"title":"","content":"Against any other setting Neolithic Mage would have won for me so hard. Viking Werewolves is just to awesome and significant a period to not have in the book. It really should be a major foundational period for them and the whole gameline stands to gain greatly from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T15:10:51-08:00","id":388982,"title":"","content":"Man I would kill (not really <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) for Neolithic: Anything. That it could be Mage is just icing on the cake (though my first choice for pre-history would be vampire).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T16:45:43-08:00","id":389112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=388767#post388767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue, helvetica, arial, lucida grande, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I love <b>Mage</b>, but <b>Werewolf</b> need it's love also. As mine modern <b>Wolfs</b> game is set on the North of Sweden, on the ruins of old werewolf-Vikings settlement, I feel a game need more mine vote. Especially, as original setting for <b>Werewolf</b>, 1970s New York, is a bit joke, in comparison with <b>Mage</b> one <i>To The Strongest</i>. So mine vote goes to Viking werewolves, but if it will lost, I win also with <b>Mage</b> one Era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you want Old Norse stuff, you should've set it in southern Sweden. The Vikings never went that far north, it was full of Sami, and no one to plunder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> That said, yeah, I also went for the Werewolf stuff. Mostly because I think the medieval stuff has more import on today than stone age things do.<br /> Also, I'm a wee bit of an Old Norse nerd. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:18:25-08:00","id":389140,"title":"","content":"Honestly, this makes me feel like:<br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/000/538/731/0fc.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Seriously, both would be awesome settings and I honestly feel they both should be in the book. Could we maybe get a follow up stretch to get the runner up in the book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:27:01-08:00","id":389145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=388982#post388982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man I would kill (not really <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) for Neolithic: Anything. That it could be Mage is just icing on the cake (though my first choice for pre-history would be vampire).</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as prehistory is concerned, I've read an awful lot about Iron Age Britain, and would be keen to do something set then and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-01-2015, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:52:20-08:00","id":389163,"title":"","content":"Voted Mage but would not be dissapointed if it turns out to be Viking Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T22:28:38-08:00","id":389455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=388767#post388767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica neue, helvetica, arial, lucida grande, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I love <b>Mage</b>, but <b>Werewolf</b> need it's love also. As mine modern <b>Wolfs</b> game is set on the North of Sweden, on the ruins of old werewolf-Vikings settlement, I feel a game need more mine vote. Especially, as original setting for <b>Werewolf</b>, 1970s New York, is a bit joke, in comparison with <b>Mage</b> one <i>To The Strongest</i>. So mine vote goes to Viking werewolves, but if it will lost, I win also with <b>Mage</b> one Era. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Do we really need to disparage the work of the people who wrote these sections?<br /> <br /> The Werewolf Dark Era is the best thing I've seen written for Werewolf in a long time. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T04:07:53-08:00","id":389640,"title":"","content":"By the way, when does the poll close?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T05:14:13-08:00","id":389702,"title":"","content":"When the kickstarter hits the stretch goal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T05:42:03-08:00","id":389730,"title":"","content":"Is there a clarification on what we're exactly talking about for &quot;Neolithic&quot;, since that's a period crossing some four thousand years and a lot of distinct social models.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:13:04-08:00","id":389861,"title":"","content":"One of my best friends is much taken with werewolves and vikings and I used to play games set in roughly the wild west era a lot so this was a very tough choice. Even so, I voted Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:23:35-08:00","id":389872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=389730#post389730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a clarification on what we're exactly talking about for &quot;Neolithic&quot;, since that's a period crossing some four thousand years and a lot of distinct social models.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As you say, could be all sorts of places and times. The Neolithic is everything between the development of agriculture and the widespread use of metallurgy. It's an <i>ocean</i> of time, larger than the timespan of all the other Eras put together. The last known human species other than our own died out around the start of it. <br /> <br /> You could look at the first cities - and I have friends who are doing the research on early settlements in Syria (as much as that's possible nowadays) - you could look at the height of the Stone Circle builders across North-West Europe; Stonehenge was three or four monuments built on top of one another. You could look at what it's like in the vast spaces between, where the largest human settlement you'll ever see is a collection of huts.<br /> <br /> Big topic. If it wins the vote, we'll start narrowing it down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:26:05-08:00","id":390285,"title":"","content":"Forgive a novice but what will Neolithic mean... Anyone that would care to speculate.<br /> <br /> Is this before the Fall? Before the Abyss? Before watchtowers? Is it after the Fall but while the Orders are supposedly isolated from each other? Will the Seers be unknown by the Orders members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:38:37-08:00","id":390301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big topic. If it wins the vote, we'll start narrowing it down.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was thinking that narrowing might help my choice. I'll look at the list again. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Johnny</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it after the Fall but while the Orders are supposedly isolated from each other? Will the Seers be unknown by the Orders members?</div> </div> </div> </div> Short answer; all of history is after the Fall, and the Orders were formed in the 4th century BCE. There's probably barely even magical philosophies yet, unless it touches on the Baalim of Kush (the first Scelesti).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:43:31-08:00","id":390303,"title":"","content":"Everything is after Fall, as the Fall didn't happen in any recorded or unrecorded part of the current timeline. The current Mage Dark Eras (To the Strongest) is set before the Orders or the Seers were a thing, so that's a given too in a previous (very previous!) period like Neolithic.<br /> <br /> Most probably we will see a world where magic (and everything) is new an open to discovery. There's all left to learn. And that's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:44:16-08:00","id":390404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most probably we will see a world where magic (and everything) is new an open to discovery. There's all left to learn. And that's awesome. </div> </div> </div>I could see the opposite. The neolithic is at least six thousand years and a lot of the major changes to human society are incredibly slow. That means a lot of fairly slow paced continuity; your society and lifestyle will be pretty similiar as the one your parents were in, and theirs and so on. Even then, humans aren't new to the world, there's a gulf of time before the Neolithic too.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, neolithic magi visiting a monumental Atlantean Ruin is something I want to run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T20:45:17-08:00","id":390928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=389872#post389872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As you say, could be all sorts of places and times. The Neolithic is everything between the development of agriculture and the widespread use of metallurgy. It's an <i>ocean</i> of time, larger than the timespan of all the other Eras put together. The last known human species other than our own died out around the start of it.<br /> <br /> You could look at the first cities - and I have friends who are doing the research on early settlements in Syria (as much as that's possible nowadays) - you could look at the height of the Stone Circle builders across North-West Europe; Stonehenge was three or four monuments built on top of one another. You could look at what it's like in the vast spaces between, where the largest human settlement you'll ever see is a collection of huts.<br /> <br /> Big topic. If it wins the vote, we'll start narrowing it down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It should make for a good resource for cossover purposes too - as it will reflect (for example) the nature of the Awakened when Irem is in ascendancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:13:57-08:00","id":391041,"title":"","content":"Finally, a setting where I can fully leverage the imagery of two mages dueling by picking up a handful of stones and throwing them at each other, one at a time.<br /> <br /> One stone is enhanced to have the kinetic force of a meteorite, another becomes a snarling tiger, another tears through the threshold, a beacon to a horde of spirits. The last and most dreadful is enchanted with the weight of Now, and upon striking its target, pins them down in time, knocking them over as the world rushes headlong over them. It takes only a moment to shove this stone aside and stand back up...a moment, and five thousand years. The loser of the duel regains their footing and looks up at the glowing billboard in front of them, not yet aware how much mundane and supernatural attention they are in danger of drawing in downtown Tokyo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T01:17:30-08:00","id":391142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=390928#post390928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It should make for a good resource for cossover purposes too - as it will reflect (for example) the nature of the Awakened when Irem is in ascendancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give all background, Awakened magic is really just on force of magic among others. Iremic being one of the other notable ones while the other &quot;hedge traditions&quot; are there as well (Skin-Changers, non-Awakened Shamans, etc).<br /> <br /> So while the population may be &quot;awakened&quot; to low magic, they are not Awakened to the stuff that the Awakened can do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T01:21:40-08:00","id":391144,"title":"","content":"Just the thought of playing characters that can be part of the discurs that would eventually form the different Orders makes me want to through more money at the kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Okay so the Fallen World is set, what about things that haven't been invented yet? Will they technically be magic? (just tell me if I'm going off-topic here and I'll stop). Will say farming not be possible without magic (since it hasn't become part of the Lie/Fallen World yet)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T02:15:03-08:00","id":391167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Johnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=391144#post391144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just the thought of playing characters that can be part of the discurs that would eventually form the different Orders makes me want to through more money at the kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Okay so the Fallen World is set, what about things that haven't been invented yet? Will they technically be magic? (just tell me if I'm going off-topic here and I'll stop). Will say farming not be possible without magic (since it hasn't become part of the Lie/Fallen World yet)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference between the Mesolithic and Neolithic is the invention of farming, so... No.<br /> <br /> Also, this is not Mage: The Ascension. Science that hasn't been invented yet is not magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T02:19:38-08:00","id":391170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay so the Fallen World is set, what about things that haven't been invented yet? Will they technically be magic? </div> </div> </div>Unless it includes some radical rewrite of the setting assumptions, no; that's really more Ascension cosmology. The parameters of the Fallen World are basically the same as the real world; if you could somehow move a nuclear weapon back to the Neolithic, it'd still work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will say farming not be possible without magic (since it hasn't become part of the Lie/Fallen World yet)? </div> </div> </div>The Neolithic is the development of agriculture. It's more that you can't actually farm if you don't have domesticated crops or animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:22:22-08:00","id":391238,"title":"","content":"Although I think Scelesti mythology says that the Baalim were the first ones to teach Sleepers farming (with the idea that they needed to learn how to work the land rather than pray to it), but the accuracy of that is probably up in the air.<br /> <br /> There would probably have been occasions where local mages used their powers to aid in some food productivity, and one might devise scenarios where the actions of mages helped people to figure farming out (or provided a safe and stable environment to settle into it), but it was always possible for somebody to plant seeds and cultivate the resulting plants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:25:17-08:00","id":391343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=389872#post389872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> Big topic. If it wins the vote, we'll start narrowing it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...<br /> <br /> Now that Neolithic Mage has won, can we get a clue in to the development process? See how you're narrowing this down?<br /> <br /> Because I'm excited as hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:28:52-08:00","id":391349,"title":"","content":"I second this! Set it in the cradle of civilization? I'd say the Harrapan culture, but we know so little about the Indus Valley civilizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:56:57-08:00","id":391361,"title":"","content":"I'd love something to do with Stonehenge, even if it's a sidebar (for the purely selfish reason that it'd be a lot easier for me to poach stuff for my modern game if it's in the UK as opposed to South Asia).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T08:51:07-08:00","id":391474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=391167#post391167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, this is not Mage: The Ascension. Science that hasn't been invented yet is not magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right... thanks, I still get a lot of the concepts mixed up in my head between the two.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the clarification, I'll go and reread some of the core book before I bother anyone with things like this again :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4908-dreaming-johnny","name":"Dreaming Johnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:14:12-08:00","id":391601,"title":"","content":"It is easy to get confused. I do: in all times and in all places.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:15:02-08:00","id":396017,"title":"","content":"I like the Alexander setting but the Neolithic era sounds meh. <br /> <br /> I'm sure you guys will surprise me though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:25:57-08:00","id":396034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=391343#post391343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...<br /> <br /> Now that Neolithic Mage has won, can we get a clue in to the development process? See how you're narrowing this down?<br /> <br /> Because I'm excited as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth a blog in a little while, yeah. I had my first conversations with Rich about it last night. We may be going for the Windmill Hill Culture and Stonehenge I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:51:46-08:00","id":396047,"title":"","content":"So Stonehenge? Well, the nearest Neolithic culture to historical times. I'm a bit... not excited?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:55:04-08:00","id":396049,"title":"","content":"As fun as 'Mage: the Flintstones' sounds, I think I'm going to have to pass on this one. <br /> <br /> I don't why but none of these eras sounds the slightest bit interesting. I think its because I'm still a relative newcomer to the World of Darkness and I have yet to explore/exhaust all the 'conventional' themes and settings for the game lines. All this seems designed for jaded aficionados who just want some of the craziness of the old world of darkness's historical settings. I'm perfectly happy with the 'boring' stuff. <br /> <br /> It's a massive shame that the Second Sight chapter is lost to the mists, since that the original book and that chapter held real promise. I know from the experience of my gaming group that SS was very well regarded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Have you seen him? </i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1000-mistere","name":"MisterE","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1000_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T02:59:56-08:00","id":396051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=396034#post396034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's worth a blog in a little while, yeah. I had my first conversations with Rich about it last night. We may be going for the Windmill Hill Culture and Stonehenge I.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *does math* Would that mean we're already post fall of Irem, then? Though still predating the cities of the Indus River valley?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:48:09-08:00","id":396352,"title":"","content":"IF we go for that, it'd be a few centuries post-Irem, but still before any mummies first arose. Might go earlier, though, or elsewhere. We're still looking!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T10:16:06-08:00","id":396469,"title":"","content":"Irem's bleeding ancient, and it's fall is implied to have actually crippled early human civilizations to some degree.<br /> <br /> Just a note(not to the devs,who know way more than I do on the matter)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T12:42:35-08:00","id":396646,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping the Yellow River Valley gets some love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T22:54:03-08:00","id":397228,"title":"","content":"The reference in &quot;To the Strongest&quot; to this being the first time the Exarchs start getting worried about the power of earthly Awakened, and thus the beginning of the Seers of the Throne as a reaction to the growing together of the Diamond Orders, resulted in a headcanon for me, that's only true in terms of the continuously existing Iron Pyramid.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, the Awakened of &quot;Harappa&quot; and &quot;Mohenja-Daro&quot; in the Indus River Valley were one of the closest attempts to recreating the glories of Atlantis, and loyalists of the Exarchs did exist in that era as a result as well as a response - but those cults vanished after the collapse of said civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T20:49:09-08:00","id":398354,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping we see Gobekli Tepe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T21:30:56-08:00","id":398389,"title":"","content":"Yes, if we go by the Neolit, we should focus on really <b>old</b> one, not the &quot;almost historical&quot; one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:03:22-08:00","id":398430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=398389#post398389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if we go by the Neolit, we should focus on really <b>old</b> one, not the &quot;almost historical&quot; one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well they're only &quot;almost historic&quot; for the fact that stuff that was &quot;almost historic&quot; was happening in the Middle East, North Africa, and Indus River Valley. The British Isles at the time were as shrouded in Stone Age mystery 3000 BCE, as those regions had been 5,000 years previous. It's a locational measurement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:05:48-08:00","id":398431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=398354#post398354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping we see Gobekli Tepe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the only problem there is that might fall under the purview of the Nameless Empire based on its timing and location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T22:48:13-08:00","id":398462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=398431#post398431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the only problem there is that might fall under the purview of the Nameless Empire based on its timing and location.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit of a ways East for the Nameless Empire, but that's the rub with ill-defined psuedo-historical political entities, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T23:42:32-08:00","id":398503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=398431#post398431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only problem there is that might fall under the purview of the Nameless Empire based on its timing and location.</div> </div> </div> </div>As astonishing as it is to say this, Gobleki Tepi predates Irem to a significant degree, according to my shoddy pencil-drawn timeline. Perhaps not the Shan'iatu, however! They were around for a REALLY long time and the story of Irem only begins in the last chapter, really!<br /> <br /> It's all really vague but more or less by my notes this is what I got from Decieved : In the 'first age', the Shan'iatu were crazy powerful. This is the era before they discover necromancy and get kind of corrupted by it. They discover humans and create a civilization with them that is NOT Irem ; this may, in fact, be the origin of Gobleki Tepi and other sites. This culture would be a more 'pure' version of the Nameless Empire, theoretically, as it would predate much of the later corruption the Shan'iatu clearly experienced interacting with Ammut.The end of the first age seems to be when the Shan'iatu try to test the might of Anpu and get unmade. Who knows how long they were gone? When Anpu unmakes you, it might take a while to reform your Temakh!... so from the perspective of human followers, they must have seemed to just vanish. Whatever happened to those cultures is very mysterious, right?<br /> <br /> When they came back, some are humbled and they become students of Anpu. They learn more about Necromancy. This is the second age, where the Shan'iatu understand necromancy and accept (at least temporarily) that they aren't allowed into the afterlife. A few of them bow to Anpu and learn many secrets, but others have learned concepts like 'hate' and dislike Anpu immensely. Listening to Ammut, even just a little bit, has changed them already quit impressively.<br /> <br /> At some point the masters of the Shell decide to 'educate the other Shan'iatu', and we have no idea what that means, because they don't really go into it. I like to imagine that the Shan'iatu were fighting over something at this point, quarreling amongst themselves in a crucial moment when they should have been minding the store. The Master Amkhata appears and almost destroys the world. This is a huge, huge deal that marks the end of the 'Second Age' of the Shan'iatu. This is implied to be a massive ecological disaster that all but wipes out humanity (I usually pin it to the desertification of the the Sahara, circa 7000BC). The Shan'iatu 'die' again (or sleep), and when they return, they are 'wounded'. These wounds never go away.<br /> <br /> SO! The Shan'iatu sleep for a long-ass time before they wake up, sacrificing an entire tribe of people to do so. At this point it's mentioned that those who are wounded are more powerful than those who aren't (strange huh?). These Shan'iatu are a lot less powerful and not at all the Gods they used to be. Still, they're pretty smart and potent cuz they manage to kill Azar in a big ritual that's sorta a foreshadowing of the Rite of Return, when you think about it?<br /> <br /> When it fails they go hide in the sand for 'centuries' so that's even more time. Eventually Anpu guilt trips them (if that's accurate) and they come back. THEN they finally, finally form the idea of Irem. This is not the first civilization the Shan'iatu attemped! It's more than likely not at all as ideologically close to the original intentions of Azar as previous efforts, either.<br /> <br /> So, Irem... believe it or not... in the timeline I've jotted down for Mummy that has all of these ages outlined, is actually pretty recent! As crazy as that is. Lotsa epic stuff in the world of Mummy happened before them, it's got a very rich almost Tolkein esque background which is really cool.<br /> <br /> Because the Shan'iatu are described as having spread all around the world in this early age, I like to say they scattered all around the world and kinda monstrously bred humans into a perfect 'toy breed' like we do now with dogs... which is why many other types of hominids die out rather suddenly, including the neanderthals. Humans in that period live like pets because all powerful Shan'iatu obsess over removing suffering and never letting people die or experience emotional or physical pain. This doesn't work out all the time, as you might imagine. Early Shan'iatu while well intentioned and all powerful understand humans not at all, while later Shan'iatu understand humans great but also are much less powerful and prone to wanting to have sex with and/or enslave humans rather than shelter them.<br /> <br /> <i>TL;DR - Gobleki Tepi is really, really old and way older than Irem, though it might be evidence of a 'prot-Irem' attempted by much less corrupted Shan'iatu in prehistory.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 02-09-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:31:41-08:00","id":398752,"title":"","content":"I think both ancient neolithic and near-the-end neolithic could be both good.<br /> <br /> Ancent neolithic could gave us an image of mages society at its very beginning, in a time before the aparition of big cities, when mages are still discoverng what they can do without any kind of organizated society. It would be a very original approximation.<br /> <br /> But modern neolithic in Middle East coul offer us a very great opportunities for crossovers. Mage in Mesopotamia about 5000 bC could give us some potential crossovers with werewolf and Mummy. Irem was the great potency of the time, how did mesopotamian mages reacted to the invading forces of Irem. Which was the relationship among them and Irem sorcerers? And, later, in Summer, werewolves will rule. How was that process? How did they obtain that supremacy?<br /> Also, Dave has told us first magical society were the Scelesti of Kish. That chapter could give us some insight about the &quot;prehistory&quot; of Mesopotamian Scelesti. how did they began the dominant force of mesopotamian mages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:41:39-08:00","id":399480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Dave has told us first magical society were the Scelesti of Kish. That chapter could give us some insight about the &quot;prehistory&quot; of Mesopotamian Scelesti. how did they began the dominant force of mesopotamian mages?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not dominant over mages; mages who organised to become dominant over a society of Sleepers. They used a combination of developing agricultural techniques and distributing Investments so that every commoner could live like a god; this necessitated slave raids on surrounding cities for the sake of collecting people who could actually clean the toilets, which ultimately brought other mages together to destroy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:55:28-08:00","id":399488,"title":"","content":"I am really curious how they do neolothic mage, as IIRC this is the stone age, the age when people are slowly stop being cavemen, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T20:17:09-08:00","id":399866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=399480#post399480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not dominant over mages; mages who organised to become dominant over a society of Sleepers. They used a combination of developing agricultural techniques and distributing Investments so that every commoner could live like a god; this necessitated slave raids on surrounding cities for the sake of collecting people who could actually clean the toilets, which ultimately brought other mages together to destroy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the aclaration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T23:38:49-08:00","id":400076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=399488#post399488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really curious how they do neolothic mage, as IIRC this is the stone age, the age when people are slowly stop being cavemen, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Neolithic era does include the agricultural revolution that allows the shift from hunter gatherer to a more settled (though much more labor-intensive) lifestyle. Where along that continuum the setting will focus, we have no idea.<br /> <br /> That said - the strereotypical &quot;cave-man&quot; image is Paleolithic, not Neolithic. Humans have buildings, pottery, broad tool use, etc etc in this era. But yes, those tools are mostly going to still be stone, rather than metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T01:29:44-08:00","id":400111,"title":"","content":"I think that whatever Neolithic setting it is, it should be focused on playability first and being an interesting analysis second. The idea of what mages were like in the very earliest forms of human society might be interesting as a concept, but I think its gameplay options may be limited. That's not to say it's impossible, but there might be an opportunity cost at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:44:18-08:00","id":400258,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about Neanderthals...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T06:57:09-08:00","id":400275,"title":"","content":"There were no neanderthals in neolithic. They were extincted almost 20.000years before.<br /> <br /> But... Rhmoals may be? In some Mage and Hunter books there hacve been references to Rhmoals, either as a magical society that predated atlantis or as a servants of the Awakened in Artlantis. May be they could be the neanderthal mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T07:15:39-08:00","id":400289,"title":"","content":"Oups...sorry..but yeah Rhmoals could be last neanderthal mage survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T17:05:45-08:00","id":412218,"title":"","content":"One good chronicle frame for Neolithic Mage could be going the Ancient Astronaut/nephilim/Enochian mythology/Flood pseudohistory path spelled out in books like Uriel's Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uriel%27s_Machine\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3c/Uriel%27s_Machine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uriel%27s_Machine\" target=\"_blank\"> Uriel's Machine - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uriel%27s_Machine\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uriel%27s_Machine </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5109-mgrasso","name":"mgrasso","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:43:46-08:00","id":419685,"title":"","content":"If mage cosmology is officially accurate, there can, <i>and really ought to be</i>, anachronisms throughout the timeline, most <b>especially</b> around emergent civilization and the beginnings of various important truths. Philosophical golden ages would be pivotal times, as would any technological shifts between ages. The logoi would be in play at any such time, and dramatically so. Ananke are related, as well.<br /> <br /> One type of anachronism would be the otherwise seemingly random discovery of an important truth that might be rediscovered later. A civilization could bounce into a golden age and grow powerful through the efforts of a sage or a lineage of sages, only to collapse. These could be seen as inspiration and insight or as the effects of truths imprinted on the timeline in previous cosmological edits making their way known.<br /> <br /> Another thing that would be interesting to consider would be bygones, and how they relate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:54:18-08:00","id":419712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419685#post419685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If mage cosmology is officially accurate, there can, <i>and really ought to be</i>, anachronisms throughout the timeline, most <b>especially</b> around emergent civilization and the beginnings of various important truths. Philosophical golden ages would be pivotal times, as would any technological shifts between ages. The logoi would be in play at any such time, and dramatically so. Ananke are related, as well.<br /> <br /> One type of anachronism would be the otherwise seemingly random discovery of an important truth that might be rediscovered later. A civilization could bounce into a golden age and grow powerful through the efforts of a sage or a lineage of sages, only to collapse. These could be seen as inspiration and insight or as the effects of truths imprinted on the timeline in previous cosmological edits making their way known.<br /> <br /> Another thing that would be interesting to consider would be bygones, and how they relate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny part is that if it isn't officially accurate, there's even more wonderful anachronisms going around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:18:01-08:00","id":419739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419712#post419712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The funny part is that if it isn't officially accurate, there's even more wonderful anachronisms going around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[