" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird shit not happening there means even more is Weird shit happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>And more for the sake of being weird shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T23:11:00-08:00","id":419873,"title":"","content":"I hope its crossover side-bar concerning <b>Mummy</b> is still interesting. This would be before the first Sothic turn, but surely the Deceived were up and about even before then? After all, their masters did not intend for them to rest in a tomb for eternity, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T01:01:00-08:00","id":419961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419873#post419873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope its crossover side-bar concerning <b>Mummy</b> is still interesting. This would be before the first Sothic turn, but surely the Deceived were up and about even before then? After all, their masters did not intend for them to rest in a tomb for eternity, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on when exactly in the Neolithic we're looking at, we may be predating Irem or even during its existence (unless the timeline is as fucked as it seems). Could be nice if there are some of the demons from Duat showing up, and maybe hint at ties between Ammut and the Abyss.<br /> <br /> I'm excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T01:37:08-08:00","id":419973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419961#post419961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on when exactly in the Neolithic we're looking at, we may be predating Irem or even during its existence (unless the timeline is as fucked as it seems). Could be nice if there are some of the demons from Duat showing up, and maybe hint at ties between Ammut and the Abyss.<br /> <br /> I'm excited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more interested to see what kind of Hunter Compacts are up and while the Uratha are still just trying to figure out what happened to their paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T02:13:34-08:00","id":419983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419973#post419973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more interested to see what kind of Hunter Compacts are up and while the Uratha are still just trying to figure out what happened to their paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Forsaken might be operating as an earlier version of the Ur-Sag who ruled Bau, perhaps acting as individual patrons for some tribes in much the same way that totems work for packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T02:51:16-08:00","id":419991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=419983#post419983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Forsaken might be operating as an earlier version of the Ur-Sag who ruled Bau, perhaps acting as individual patrons for some tribes in much the same way that totems work for packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the change in pack structure, entire tribes might be brought under the patronage of a spirit, with a group of Uratha acting as a check on it's power... and it's spokesperson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T18:15:10-08:00","id":420941,"title":"","content":"If certain branches of early humans are more vulnerable to spiritual influences and/or attacks, they would be valued more than others. If the more powerful spirits can punch through the gauntlet more frequently, you have a good basis for tribal gods, gods of places, and so forth.<br /> This could be related, actually, making certain people living channels for patron spirits, for example, would make shaman and religions make a lot of sense in the setting.<br /> The low and high magic, shamans, uratha, and such could all be various factions. Some groups would work together. The pattern of mages reigning and falling could be repeated in a thousand petty kingdoms, but still be rivaled by, e.g. uratha tribes and/or those protected by Dreamspeakers. Isolated super-nature would be more rare.<br /> <br /> That would make this a really nifty setting for general crossover: Kingdoms of the gods and heroes. Those empowered by supernatural patrons would be particularly potent figures, even...<br /> <br /> I kid, but a more serious take on the themes in Exalted really <i>could</i> fit this era in a compelling way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:50:03-07:00","id":460539,"title":"","content":"Well, I just pressed &quot;send&quot; on the Outline for Neolithic Awakening, tentatively called &quot;The Bull and The Bird&quot;. In the end, we did not go for Stonehenge. The addition of 5k of Werewolf material thanks to a special backer tier, plus my reading turning out to be something of a forced march down memory lane into my own career as an archaeologist, settled it.<br /> <br /> We're going to 5500 BCE. We're going to the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vin%C4%8Da_culture\" target=\"_blank\">Vin\u010da people in Southeastern Europe</a> - the first people to invent writing, which they only used for magical purposes (hiiiiiiigh speeeeeeech), the first people to invent metallurgy, a culture that lasted near-on 2000 years and influenced everything from the megalith builders in the West, the Minoans to the South and the Sumerians in the East. A people whose principle inter-town trade was in ritual paraphernalia.<br /> <br /> 7000 years plus change ago. The World is still Fallen from the Time Before Time, but this is an ambitious setting, and I'm really glad people voted for it with such fervor.<br /> <br /> Before the Vampires were anything other than Strix-possessed corpses.<br /> Before the shan'iatu built Irem<br /> Before the Sundering.<br /> There was something else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T17:59:19-07:00","id":460541,"title":"","content":"Wait, <i>BEFORE</i> the Sundering?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"