s://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:36:21-07:00","id":524179,"title":"","content":"The historical settings for Mage are probably my favourite setting choices coupled with my favourite line (with 2ed only making that more of the case!) Very excited.<br /> <br /> Will there be any setting links between To The Strongest and Neolithic? It would be cool for there to be a couple of Easter eggs, if nothing else! #begging","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:41:42-07:00","id":524183,"title":"","content":"I don't think so - The Bull &amp; Bird is set some 5300 years before To The Strongest; more than twice as far as To The Strongest is to the modern day. Any links that you could spot (beyond both the wise ones in the Neolithic and the magi in TTS being <i>mages</i>) would be nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 05-22-2015, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T01:45:46-07:00","id":524185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=524183#post524183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so - The Bull &amp; Bird is set some 5300 years before To The Strongest; more than twice as far as To The Strongest is to the modern day. Any links that you could spot (beyond both the wise ones in the Neolithic and the magi in TTS being <i>mages</i>) would be nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>... maybe something with the Aeons... I mean it's plausible... vaguely...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T03:06:29-07:00","id":524199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=524183#post524183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so - The Bull &amp; Bird is set some 5300 years before To The Strongest; more than twice as far as To The Strongest is to the modern day. Any links that you could spot (beyond both the wise ones in the Neolithic and the magi in TTS being <i>mages</i>) would be nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fair point. I might include some Neolithic tombs or something in a To The Strongest game, though, just out of a desire to reference the material, if only at a great distance.<br /> <br /> That is, if it's appropriate. Have to give it a read first! Very excited though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T04:27:44-07:00","id":524239,"title":"","content":"Doubly excited, it seems!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:23:37-07:00","id":527085,"title":"","content":"Given that we've got a 5300-year gap between the Bull &amp; the Bird and To the Strongest, we could very easily have some sort of \u201cOrders\u201d that were founded in this Neolithic culture, but died out and passed into the mists of time long before the more recent historical setting. And they may bear no resemblance to anything that came later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T09:32:59-07:00","id":528832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">we could very easily have some sort of \u201cOrders\u201d that were founded in this Neolithic culture, but died out and passed into the mists of time long before the more recent historical setting. And they may bear no resemblance to anything that came later.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I'd go with the &quot;not resemble anything that comes after&quot; thing myself. Probably wind up with some god-kings or priests over great Mesopotamian temple complexes more than Orders. Which reminds me, has Dave said anything about this being the kind of time in which Cxaxa Queraphas was active?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:38:17-07:00","id":528950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=527085#post527085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they may bear no resemblance to anything that came later.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Supernal symbols of orders already existed. So I think that while they were very different from modern orders, orders still were proto-Ladder, proto-Arrow, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:47:17-07:00","id":529136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daimon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=528950#post528950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Supernal symbols of orders already existed. So I think that while they were very different from modern orders, orders still were proto-Ladder, proto-Arrow, etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Orders as Supernal Mandates are kinda going out with 2e. While aspects of their Symbolism likely will be present no matter the period, the idea that &quot;the Diamond will always exist because the Atlantean ideals if such cultures impose them onto reality&quot; is not a thing in 2e. Dave explained that this was being dropped (or significantly diminished), and pointed to the Banishers as &quot;another Supernally enforced group like the other Orders&quot; as part of the reason for this. <br /> <br /> I mean, if you look at To The Strongest, there are definitely elements of the modern orders (which makes sense, considering that this is when they start to form). But at the same time, we don't even have the split between the Seers and Silver Ladder, and we know that the Mysterium starts as two seperate Orders. <br /> <br /> So, while I could see mages taking on roles that may line up with different aspects of the Orders during the Neolithic Era (a tribes leader, or a guardian of the tribe) I think that these are going to be relatively unique to each culture and lacking any part of a greater organization. This is a periods where most cultures are just developing specialization of labor and settling in cities for the first time, so the most you might have is local organizations of mages who likely would be more like cabals then orders. So yes, while some people may take on roles that line up with the orders, the Orders themselves likely won't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:25:43-07:00","id":529270,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that this is supposed to be a time predating the Sundering; at least a few mages are going to be worried about dealing with all of those spirits walking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:55:26-07:00","id":529301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=529270#post529270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that this is supposed to be a time predating the Sundering; at least a few mages are going to be worried about dealing with all of those spirits walking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Imagine the role of a Thyrsus when the spirits are there amongst you, rather than beings from another realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:43:31-07:00","id":529398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=529301#post529301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. Imagine the role of a Thyrsus when the spirits are there amongst you, rather than beings from another realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless this changed in Werewolf 2nd Edition, I think that technically most spirits will still be in the Shadow, and most humans in the material, as wolf beasts (and maybe stranger things) patrol the Border Marches separating them. But I agree that there will probably be more spirits in the material world, than in the normal setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:58:50-07:00","id":529409,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I was employing a bit of hyperbole there, although I do think that the distinction between Gauntlet and Border Marches at least lends itself to a more widespread awareness of the spirit world and the concept of transitioning to it instead of forcing a hole through a barrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:16:13-07:00","id":529417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orders as Supernal Mandates are kinda going out with 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's a half-and-half thing; the idea that, in all times and places, groups resembling the four (or five, even) Orders inevitably arise from imperceptible influences won't be a thing, and there'll be more emphasis on the historical background of some of the particular terminology and rituals and metaphysical models. But at the same time, investigations into what is perceived under Active and Focused Mage Sight and looking into uncanny ruins will give some insight into the idea of archetypal social roles and the power that can be drawn thereof. One doesn't need to be anything close to a thearch. with the Elemental Precepts and the Convocations and the Lex Magica to start approaching the rudiments of &quot;adopting a vizier role in society comes with some perks to magic&quot;, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:18:16-07:00","id":529418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=529398#post529398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless this changed in Werewolf 2nd Edition, I think that technically most spirits will still be in the Shadow, and most humans in the material, as wolf beasts (and maybe stranger things) patrol the Border Marches separating them. But I agree that there will probably be more spirits in the material world, than in the normal setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently before the Sundering, people were free to cross to the Hisil, and spirits to the mortal world, providing Father Wolf didn't object.<br /> <br /> 'The Forsaken call the vanished world before the Sundering \u201cPangaea,\u201d and describe it as a universe where spirit and flesh could more freely commingle. Humans could wander into the quiet places of the world and cross the Border Marches into the Shadow, while spirits could freely enter the world of Flesh to gather Essence.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T20:22:01-07:00","id":529555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=529417#post529417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's a half-and-half thing; the idea that, in all times and places, groups resembling the four (or five, even) Orders inevitably arise from imperceptible influences won't be a thing, and there'll be more emphasis on the historical background of some of the particular terminology and rituals and metaphysical models. But at the same time, investigations into what is perceived under Active and Focused Mage Sight and looking into uncanny ruins will give some insight into the idea of archetypal social roles and the power that can be drawn thereof. One doesn't need to be anything close to a thearch. with the Elemental Precepts and the Convocations and the Lex Magica to start approaching the rudiments of &quot;adopting a vizier role in society comes with some perks to magic&quot;, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, agreed. I was speaking more of the first part you described (The &quot;Orders inevitably arise from imperceptible influences&quot; bit). That was were I was going with my post. I don't deny that elements may exist from a pre-existing culture, or that the Symbolism of the Archtypes posited by the orders can't be discerned and pieced together from studying the Supernal. Just that the Order's themselves don't appear no matter what Ex Nihilo, but arose from the natural evolution of mage culture and the study of the supernal, which in turn arose from the cultural development in the sleeper cultures (if there is no concept of specialized labor, then why would Mages know what they were looking for/at?*). Once they did have a point of reference and built on these, they still would have to have to build more upon it to formalize it (like any philosophical model) and then have to convince others that it is an accurate model (Once you encounter them). While mages had advantages over sleepers in achieving advancement of theses studies and their spread, there are still limitations that mages will face, as we have seen from the &quot;To the Strongest&quot; chapter, where more unified theories are just beginning to be posited. <br /> <br /> <br /> *This is associated with something I pointed out on another part of the forum:<br /> A mage using forces may be able to see and interact with Radio Waves, but before the sleeper discovery of what those waves are, the Mage can only understand them through the lens of the those waves' Supernal Symbolism, which might not give them a &quot;scientific&quot; insight about what thoae waves are. Essentially, the Mages would have an understanding of the radio waves and be able to understand any signal carried, but they wouldn't be able to relate what they are studying back to fallen reality since they only see it through the Symbolism of their sight and have no fallen analog to associate it with. For example, an Obrimos may think they are the wavelength of angel communication, while the other paths might see them differently as per their Path's sight, and none will see them as &quot;a part of the electromagnetic spectrum, whose long wavelength and low frequencies allow for information transmission at significant distances&quot; because that is the fallen, scientific explanation of them (yes, science also has a supernal reflection, but that is different then fallen explanations we have). The mage might see the waves as related to light, infrared or other parts of the EM, but they would likely contextualize these as part of related things in their Path.The Obrimos may see these as all parts of the Seraph of Blinding Light's manifestations in the world: the radio waves his voice, the visible spectrum his body, the infrared the warmth of his presence, etc. So, while they might create radio waves and design a &quot;rockie talkie&quot;by imbuing a stone with the ability to communicate via said waves, they likely will not be positing the theory of electromagnetism in 5300 bce, some 7100 years before sleepers came up with it, because to them, radio waves being their Supernal reflection actually would be an accurate explanation for them as they relate to the mage (&quot;Who cares about the Fallen science explanation when the Fallen World <i>is part of the Lie </i>: I have the Supernal explanation&quot;. Though the FC would beg to differ...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-27-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T03:28:31-07:00","id":535406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=524199#post524199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a fair point. I might include some Neolithic tombs or something in a To The Strongest game, though, just out of a desire to reference the material, if only at a great distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one <i>particular </i>element of the Neolithic chapter that could well turn up in To The Strongest if a Storyteller so desired, as a Mystery or prize from that past age; it's a thing that even Mages in modern-day games might find themselves motivated to seek.<br /> <br /> 'course I can't say more than that because a) spoilers and b) first draft <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T08:28:10-07:00","id":561956,"title":"","content":"We have an uptade:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-end-is-the-beginning-is-the-end-mage-the-awakening-dark-eras-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpat