en Awakenings, there has been a lost civilization in whose shadow they are cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do wonder though, when - in linear time - the first Awakeings were.<br /> <br /> One idea I had for PALEOlithic Mage, so as not to immediately turn Mages into gods of the setting with the mere ability to shape matter into shapes they want in a setting where basic tool use is cutting edge, is that the first linear time Awakened could only access the Subtle Arcana. The Gross Arcana came with the Agricultural Revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:46:16-07:00","id":568527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=568511#post568511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had missed the statement in your signature that you were a writer. My apologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm the writer on the Neolithic chapter; DaveB was kind and mad enough to let me loose on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No need to apologise!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T17:52:43-07:00","id":568556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=568527#post568527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm the writer on the Neolithic chapter; DaveB was kind and mad enough to let me loose on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No need to apologise!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great news! I love your work, and cannot wait to see what you do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T22:54:22-07:00","id":568819,"title":"","content":"I don't think we've talked about this enough...<br /> <br /> This is presumably a major setting hook for Mages independent of the Werewolf cosmology crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The world\u2019s wounds still bleed in places; pockets of shattered time, screaming ruins from impossible peoples, strange artifacts of the Time Before. Even now, they\u2019re shrinking, worn away by Dissonance when Sleepers encounter them, but the world isn\u2019t so mapped as to remove them all as entirely as they will be in later times.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:30:20-07:00","id":569085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=568522#post568522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do wonder though, when - in linear time - the first Awakeings were.<br /> <br /> One idea I had for PALEOlithic Mage, so as not to immediately turn Mages into gods of the setting with the mere ability to shape matter into shapes they want in a setting where basic tool use is cutting edge, is that the first linear time Awakened could only access the Subtle Arcana. The Gross Arcana came with the Agricultural Revolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a paleolithic Awakened would be considered a god in-setting. Definitely a mythic hero, though, tasked by the gods to fulfill a grand destiny in the benefits of his tribe or clan. Remember that, back then, the physical and spiritual world where much more interrelated; the Pangaeans where probably the first gods and caretakers of early Homo sapiens. Awakened would not have been the big fish in the pond, but the first casualty when the gods and humans were in strong disagreement. <br /> <br /> To be able to forge tool is a potential skill for the Awakened, yes, but I'd argue at that time their skills would have been put to much more pressing matters no other tribe member could accomplish, like dealing with spirits, appeasing pangaeans, looking for fresh water, weather casting, safe travel, etc. Many of these task would need for the Awakened to be far from their tribes and doing things noone else can do.<br /> <br /> Also, an important consideration is population numbers. Nomadic tribes rarely number more than a few hundreds, and even considering a much higher occurrence of Awakenings, that still makes the Awakened a thing of myth and legend, appearing only in some generations, and signaling a time of profound change for their communities, either for good or ill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:40:47-07:00","id":569092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=568202#post568202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The threads that bind the overall community of Vinca Wise are something that I did spend some time mulling over. Fortunately magic does allow for what would otherwise be the considerable obstacle of distance to be at least somewhat overcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get idea - they made first cabals in Astral Space, by the Omphalos Stone in Dreamtime, using menhirs mentioned in preview!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neolithic Chapter preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">T<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">he people </span></span></span><i>need </i><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">mages, to negotiate with the strange and uncanny, to defeat monsters, and protect them from the myriad dangers of an untamed world. The greatest symbols of this arrangement are the omphalos stones \u2013 squat menhirs marking the gathering-spot of each village. The stones protect villages from wandering spirits, and generate Demesnes in the fashion of latter-day soulstones. Each is the heart of a Pangaen god, stolen by the Wise.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-26-2015, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:07:55-07:00","id":569120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=568527#post568527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm the writer on the Neolithic chapter; DaveB was kind and mad enough to let me loose on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No need to apologise!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should get yourself an insane and/or iconic portrait picture, so people can pick you out of the crowds! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, glad to see you working on it. I like you and your writing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:31:04-07:00","id":569145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=569092#post569092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get idea - they made first cabals in Astral Space, by the Omphalos Stone in Dreamtime, using menhirs mentioned in preview!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral is certainly important to the Wise of the Vinca.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=569120#post569120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should get yourself an insane and/or iconic portrait picture, so people can pick you out of the crowds! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, glad to see you working on it. I like you and your writing!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, fine, I have added an avatar for my profile <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:51:28-07:00","id":569201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to apologise!</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it sucks when a writer is trying to engage and clarify to the furthest extent that they're capable, and get whinging for more in response. Just don't like inadvertantly contributing to that, and I appreciate your statement that the matter is being considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:54:02-07:00","id":569203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">so as not to immediately turn Mages into gods of the setting with the mere ability to shape matter into shapes they want in a setting where basic tool use is cutting edge</div> </div> </div> </div> I would imagine the most ancient humans wouldn't really have a sense of how to use such magic to shape the world in any manner not evident in nature, anymore than the Arcanum of Forces necessarily made anybody in the 13th century understand particle physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T12:43:40-07:00","id":569498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=569203#post569203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would imagine the most ancient humans wouldn't really have a sense of how to use such magic to shape the world in any manner not evident in nature, anymore than the Arcanum of Forces necessarily made anybody in the 13th century understand particle physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does... What was formerly called disbelief (don't remember its Second Edition name) destroy objects shaped by Matter though? Because if not, that brings a huge setting shift weight to any attempt at Paleolithic Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T13:22:08-07:00","id":569534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=569498#post569498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was formerly called disbelief (don't remember its Second Edition name)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T13:29:58-07:00","id":569537,"title":"","content":"And it depends. Dissonance kicks in when mortals realize something is obviously magical. It isn't based on belief so much as a recognition of a magical aspect. So even if mortals beleive in a mage's ability to make a weapon that is resistant to harm and stronger than any stone blade (i.e. a steel sword) their recognition of it as magical is itself damaging to the magical Patterning and can destroy it. <br /> <br /> Versus the modern era, where a steel sword is not obviously of magical origin (unless the sleeper knows a mage created it with magic) as steel blades can be made mundanely. It isn't like Ascension, where tech is magic now accepted by the consensus, but rather that the abyssal spark in sleepers can't pick up on Supernal magic now without the sleeper being aware of obvious magic (i.e. a breaking point). Thus, things that would have been fantastic in the past but are now mundane wouldn't trigger a sleeper unless something gives away it's magical nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-26-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T03:06:16-07:00","id":570090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does... What was formerly called disbelief (don't remember its Second Edition name) destroy objects shaped by Matter though?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Dissonance will often have difficulty even hitting spells to shape matter after the fact, if the Sleeper can't even recognise the presence of magic. Even then, if I shear excess away from a rock to make a cube, I doubt Dissonance will turn it back. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if not, that brings a huge setting shift weight to any attempt at Paleolithic Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> What do you mean specifically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:21:08-07:00","id":570673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=570090#post570090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What do you mean specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Mages being able to shape earth into tools that aren't affected by dissonance, and thus would be around for others to use, would effectively make the setting less &quot;Paleolithic&quot; by creating an unofficial form of metalwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T17:16:51-07:00","id":570727,"title":"","content":"Again, I would propose that mages in such a time <i>would not</i> shape things into tools, because they likely can't really imagine them. Maybe particle physics was the wrong comparison... the Arcanum of Matter can probably account for a lot of the needs to make a personal computer, and yet I highly doubt any mages were making such things prior to the 20th century. Even metalwork... imagine what it's like to be a prehistoric mage with no concept of metal. Even if they examine a rock that happens to contain a metal ore, how do they have the concept to really think of the metal within as a seperable thing with distinct useful properties? You're not really considering the mindset of a person in such a context who just happens to have magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T17:52:06-07:00","id":570739,"title":"","content":"Can't draw an elephant if you've never seen one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:54:34-07:00","id":570909,"title":"","content":"I guess it would depend if the supernal versions of those tools existed yet, where they could take inspiration from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T12:22:54-07:00","id":571730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=570739#post570739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't draw an elephant if you've never seen one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several metals exist freely (as in, not orebound). In particular, siver, gold and maybe copper (i'm fuzzy on this one).<br /> <br /> You still have to know those metals are somehow special to want to extract them.<br /> <br /> You <b>can't</b> transmute iron ore into iron without at least seeing the symbol of iron with Mage Sight (which require iron falling near you, and Matter Patterning). It probably reverts anyway.<br /> <br /> You probably <b>can</b> sculpt a fallen star in a bunch of knives with Matter Ruling. They probably don't revert. Those knives are kinda limited in supply and rust with time IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T13:16:44-07:00","id":571806,"title":"","content":"I am writing the second draft of the Neolithic chapter right at this very moment, and attempting to figure out if there are any sly yet evasive spoilers I can give out without getting smote by DaveB.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T21:57:59-07:00","id":572177,"title":"","content":"This is about something still about which is more a response to YEC stuff, but kind of neat. It's still a bit later than when Neolithic Mage is being set (4004 BCE v. 5500 BCE) but gives an idea of a lot of what the world is like in places. Pictures and videos might not be most accurate but it gives a good idea of how much can change in 6000 years and how much more to think about can change in 1000 years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iWjtRFNSl2s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iWjtRFNSl2s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iWjtRFNSl2s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iWjtRFNSl2s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T05:45:43-07:00","id":572550,"title":"","content":"Loose idea for Neolithic chapter - <a href=\"http://clapway.com/2015/05/21/russia-meet-taimyr-wolf-grandpa-of-the-dogs-and-wolves-123/\" target=\"_blank\">Taimyr Wolf</a> as Father Wolf original breed and grandfather of modern wolves and dogs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T06:57:55-07:00","id":572605,"title":"","content":"I think people should give very careful consideration to whether or not there are comprehensable Supernal Symbols of things that haven't been developed or made yet in their Neolithic Mage games, because that's the kind of thing that skews heavily in one direction or the other of the beliefs of certain Pentacle Orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:34:09-07:00","id":572623,"title":"","content":"See, the thing is, with the way how the supernal works, a raised symbol always existed. So even if the FC is completely right, all of the symbols that Humanity adds would always have existed. At least if IM and Omens still hold, where everything in the Supernal is considered to have always been there for the purposes of time in relation to humanity even if chronologically I changed the Supernal a minute ago (hence the whole Atlantean/Time Before never existing but having happened).<br /> <br /> Honestly, the wibbly wobbly timey-wimey nature of the Supernal, it gets really hard to discern how things come into being or if they always were there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:33:30-07:00","id":572809,"title":"","content":"Is it relevant whether those Supernal symbols exist or not? Radio waves exist, they havr always existed, but it does not mean that a prehistoric Obrimos understood what they were or what they could be used for. Likewise, a prehistoric Moros can command the earth, but would they know that mixing tin and copper makes bronze? The power of control does not necessarily come with requisite knowledge or understanding.<br /> <br /> A Moros may command metals, but why? To what purpose? Most pure metals are soft and useless for tools. Would the concept of alloys occur to a Moros? Or would they just magically tweak what's there because that's so much easier? And even if it did, would they have the requisite understanding of how to make the alloys naturally? Shape them? Cool them?<br /> <br /> It's a fallacy to think these sorts of inventions are obvious. They only seem so in hindsight; when the benefits are manifest. A Moros COULD tinker with this stuff he finds in the stone, but why? To make shiny things? His tribe has ancestors that need appeasing and stone or bone tools that need enchanting! Leave that muck to the vain chieftains and their strutting priests; there's work to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:19:02-07:00","id":572845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=572605#post572605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people should give very careful consideration to whether or not there are comprehensable Supernal Symbols of things that haven't been developed or made yet in their Neolithic Mage games, because that's the kind of thing that skews heavily in one direction or the other of the beliefs of certain Pentacle Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that extra consideration is necessary, because if there were symbols of things that did not exist yet around during the Neolithic, why wouldn't that also be the case during the present-day? That would mean that mages could explore their surroundings using mage sight looking for rare symbols of technologies that haven't been developed yet. As that doesn't seem to be the case in the present-day setting, I guess that will also no be the case in historical settings. Unless you believe that everything that can be discovered by man has already been discovered currently, which would let this argument break down, but that seems implausible to me.<br /> <br /> An easier argument would be saying that the symbol of an object or invention only exists there in the supernal world, where the related object or invention exists in the material world. This seems plausible and circumvents the problem, barring some kind of supernal inspiration of course, where part of the supernal realms manifests in the supernal world where it strictly doesn't belong. But I call that a plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:47:17-07:00","id":572982,"title":"","content":"It might work in terms of the idea that the symbols exist, but they aren't visible yet - Mages history have advanced,delving deeper and deeper into the Supernal, revealing more and more. It fits with what we know already from &quot;To the Strongest&quot;, that the Watchtowers themselves aren't well known in the era as most Awakenings haven't gotten deep enough to see them yet.<br /> <br /> Or it could just be Mages sometimes see symbols for things they have no frame of reference to understand yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T13:35:57-07:00","id":573088,"title":"","content":"The way I view it is that the Supernal Symbols are akin to another set of symbolic representations: letters, words, sentences, and languages as a whole. The reason being is that it actually ascribes to both the Diamond and FC and with what we know from IM. <br /> <br /> So letters are simple symbols. They represent a sound, and some can even represent things beyond that, such as an A being a great grade or an F being a failing grade. But when combined in certain ways, they can become a more complex entity that is itself a unique symbol: words. The letters C,H,A,R, and T all are symbolically unique, but combined form the word a charge, which itself is a unique symbol of something. The key is that those individual symbols (the letters) only have meaning if properly aligned, as &quot;thcra&quot; and &quot;arcth&quot; are just a jumble of the individual symbols and are meaningless (at least to my auto-correct<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Then these more complex symbols can be combined, there meaning changing not as significantly but still shaping an even more complex symbol: a sentence. &quot;The please chart the patients vitals an overnight medications&quot; and &quot;As you can see in the chart, 4th quarter earnings were at an all time high&quot; use chart in 2 completely ways, and these meanings, in the conetext of the other words, gives the sentence even more complex and unique meanings. But again, order and associated symbols matter, as changing the syntax or word choice can create numbed messes that are meaningless.<br /> <br /> So the Supernal is akin to this. In the very beginning, mages likely could only observe the simpler symbols, the &quot;the letters&quot;. While the idea of the device that is a radio likely was always a part of the Supernal, it is likely akin to a &quot;word&quot;: a collection of simpler force and matter symbols (radio waves, conductivity, etc.) akin to &quot;letters&quot; that when oriented properly form the symbol of the device we call a radio, a &quot;word&quot;, which itself is a more complex but unique Supernal symbol. But without even the idea of such a device, mages would never see this orientation of symbols or have the idea of such an orientation. And even more complex symbols, such as the &quot;warrior-sage&quot; or &quot;philosopher-king&quot; would not arise until significant social development from basic symbols of &quot;ideas&quot; and more complex such as &quot;dedicated specialize labor&quot; manifested from the orientation of Supernal elements.<br /> <br /> The reason this works for me is that it doesn't dismiss either the Diamond or the FC. The Diamond is right:the Supernal does contain all elements of things that ever rightfully should be, the language developed already. Yet the FC is right, as symbols arise from human development, as the patterns arise as unique symbols form from the convergence of other symbols as Humanity explores the world and create new things that draw on the existing to create something new/more complex (electromagnetism, copper and radio waves always existed, as did the potential for a radio, but the actial symbol never coalesced till someone posited and built a Radio). And it means that the timey-wimey issues of the Supernal changing aren't an issue here without also needing to explain why there were no Neolithic DJs, as the symbols were present just like words of the English language are present in a word scramble: if you don't know any words, all you see is a jumble of letters, even if the words are right in front of you, while someone who has a broad vocabulary might pick up words that weren't even supposed to be part of the puzzle. <br /> <br /> (Posted from my phone, so as always, I apologize for any typos).<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and IM: it is editing the language directly. It is making it so &quot;Thrca&quot; has a meaning now, and is not just a random jumble of symbols, or making it so &quot;Chart&quot; has additional or different meanings. It is why you need to align to world to fit your omen: you are shaping the &quot;letters&quot; and then defining that collection with the phenomenal. And like all changes or new additions, the change can take on a life of its own, or alter the use of other words associated with it. It also explains why Omens and Imperium have such drastic effects: unlike the emergence from converging symbols, these are wholesale additions that were artificially added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 06-29-2015, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T23:29:58-07:00","id":573631,"title":"","content":"Just an off hand idea for the Astral in this era, with a crossover hook - given the imminence of the basic instinctive fears that civilization is erected as bulwark against, this long ago there is no distinction between the Temenos and the Primordial Dream. The Lairs of Beasts are interspersed amongst the rest of the Temenos. Begotten can prowl the Astral as fully manifest Horrors, and do so to feed their hungers in mortal dreams (diving into Oneiroi). The Lairs are beginning to be pushed back though, as more and more space is carved out for human cultural concepts. Obviously Mages are at the forefront of this push.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T00:02:04-07:00","id":573640,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the Vinca made (mostly ornamental) things our of native copper, so they would have a decent idea of the physical properties of metal as opposed to other types of materials.<br /> <br /> It might also be worth noting that things like stone knives make poor weapons; chipped stone tools are pretty much single use, though an individual piece of flint can be worked multiple times to produce different kinds of edges for, say, butchering an animal. The cultures of Neolithic Europe were known for polished stone axes, and these were more durable (you could use one to chop down a tree), but would probably make unwieldy weapons.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the hunters of Europe already had <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holmegaard_bow\" target=\"_blank\">pretty powerful bows</a> by the Mesolithic, which could absolutely be used to kill a large animal or human being. Altering the power of a bow or the speed of an arrow seems like exactly the kind of subtle magic that Neolithic mages might use to take down powerful foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-30-2015, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T03:25:17-07:00","id":573703,"title":"","content":"So we're all in agreement that people aren't often inventing things by seeing the Supernal symbol of those things first, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T03:55:05-07:00","id":573721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=573703#post573703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're all in agreement that people aren't often inventing things by seeing the Supernal symbol of those things first, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <br /> <br /> <br /> But I could see a rock that is carved and then imbued to act as a Rockie-Talkie using Forces or Space. Wanting to be able to communicate over far distances and using magic to do so would definitely be something even a Neolithic Mage would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T15:36:29-07:00","id":574428,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why you'd necessarily need the rock; it seems like a Neolithic Mage would be more likely to think of remote communication in terms of commanding the wind to carry his voice (Forces, maybe) or causing his echo to resound in distant places (Space, probably). A rockie-talkie just seems a little... Flintstones, to me. If you really wanted an enchanted item, I would imagine that it would be something more symbolic than &quot;magic talking rock;&quot; maybe some kind of talisman with a representation of an ear or mouth engraved on it, or a little clay figure whose ear you could whisper into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-30-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T15:59:38-07:00","id":574456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=574428#post574428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you'd necessarily need the rock; it seems like a Neolithic Mage would be more likely to think of remote communication in terms of commanding the wind to carry his voice or compelling his echo to take flight and find his ally. A rockie-talkie just seems a little... Flintstones, to me. If you really wanted an enchanted item, I would imagine that it would be something more symbolic than &amp;quot;magic talking rock;&amp;quot; maybe some kind of talisman with a representation of an ear or mouth engraved on it, or a little clay figure whose ear you could whisper into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry... this stems from a different forum thread where this topic was broached before. The &quot;rockie-talkie&quot; was a joke that came from the conclusion fo that discussion. That conclusion was that while mages do have greater insight into the world, they do not have access to or understand all informarion humanity will ever know. Thus, a caveman Mage wouldn't be able to build a radio, even using magic and knowing effects, despite the Supernal defining not only what is but what could be (and thus including future tech and ideas). However, it doesn't mean they cannot utilize their knowledge and magic to create effects that possibly create an item or spell similar to things achieve with modern technology. <br /> <br /> And since the example we used was a radio, such a imbued item that mimicked a two way radio was suggested, the idea being middle age priests using sacred objects to communicate &quot;in the language of the Angels&quot; (radio waves) across great distances between the faithful. Someone asked if a caveman could use stone totems, and someone jokingly called them &quot;rockie-talkies&quot; and it was used as shorthand for the rest if the conversation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, now that I have explained the joke...<br /> <br /> Yep, I totally agree. Imbued items and artifacts have often elements reflecting their magical purpose, and i coukd see this being true since the dawn of such craftings. Sacred or symbolic items would potentially be imbued. <br /> <br /> Though not always...remember, obvious magic does not play well with sleepers, and their abyssal spark destroys magic through Dissonance. Hiding a magical item by making it appear very ordinary could help shelter it from such destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:00:20-07:00","id":574600,"title":"","content":"True, but a guy talking to a rock is going to look weird, any way you slice it; doubly so if the rock talks back. :P<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, regular people accepting that mages can do magic could be kind of a double-edged sword. On the one hand, mages are accepted as valuable members of society, and looked to for aid and council. On the other, it might make casting subtle spells more difficult, as people may be more likely to identify odd behavior as magical in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T19:24:32-07:00","id":574615,"title":"","content":"Hahaha, I wasn't even thinking of that but the image is now stuck in my head. It makes me think that thr pet rock craze was a mage's attempt to make people stop questioning his conversations with a rock.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it is an interesting issue. It makes mages moving into secrecy make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T10:50:50-07:00","id":576589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/388724-dark-eras-neolithic-chapter?p=574428#post574428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why you'd necessarily need the rock; it seems like a Neolithic Mage would be more likely to think of remote communication in terms of commanding the wind to carry his voice (Forces, maybe) or causing his echo to resound in distant places (Space, probably). A rockie-talkie just seems a little... Flintstones, to me. If you really wanted an enchanted item, I would imagine that it would be something more symbolic than &quot;magic talking rock;&quot; maybe some kind of talisman with a representation of an ear or mouth engraved on it, or a little clay figure whose ear you could whisper into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a seashell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T13:48:10-07:00","id":598654,"title":"","content":"Idea: a Obrimos Life-focused Legacy focused on farming, maybe with supplementary Forces to sense, ward against, and